    "narrative": "For today\u2019s matchup, **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier start with an elite 82.24 efficiency score. He draws a favorable outing against Walbert Ure\u00f1a, and his elite 0.461 xwOBA, paired with a significant platoon advantage, makes him the engine of our offense. Right behind him, **Junior Caminero** (78.33) and **Trea Turner** (72.36) are essential. **Junior Caminero** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Max Scherzer\u2014whose 5.08 xERA suggests he is vulnerable to the long ball\u2014while **Trea Turner** leverages a strong BvP history (49 PA) and a prime #2 slot against Sandy Alcantara. Meanwhile, **Caleb Durbin** is a sneaky play at 65.02; his efficiency is bolstered by Brandon Pfaadt\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a high-probability environment for **Caleb Durbin** to secure one of those scarce stolen bases we prioritize.\n\nThe most difficult exclusion today was **Hector Rodriguez**, who sat at a 45.39 score, narrowly missing the cutoff due to an unfavorable L/L platoon disadvantage and a looming 32% rain risk in his contest against Matthew Liberatore. Similarly, **Colt Keith** (44.95) was considered, but his matchup against Paul Skenes is statistically stifling; the combination of Skenes\u2019s elite arm and an \"Elite Hold\" profile that suppresses stolen base opportunities made him an easy fade in favor of our higher-ceiling starters. We are also monitoring the status of **Kazuma Okamoto**, whose 37.96 score puts him at risk of being a drag on our daily totals; if he drops out of the middle of the order, we will evaluate bench options to protect our game caps.",
